## Protective effect of 2D MSMOFs thin layer
The possibility of the 2D MSMOFs thin layer to protect the fragile biomacromolecules against harsh conditions was then explored.We firstly exposed the free HRP and HRP@2D MSMOFs to protease trypsin $(6\mathrm{\mg\mL^{-1}}.$ ),high concentration urea $(10~\mathsf{M})$ and heat $(80~^{\circ}\mathsf{C})$ . respectively. All of these harsh conditions give risk to unfold the proteins that leads to inactivation. The retained bioactivity, denoted as the catalytic rate conversion after different treatments, was calculated and showed in Figure 4A. After treatment by trypsin, urea and heating, the retained bioactivity of free enzymes was only $36.9\%$ ， $32.1\ \%$ and $15.6\%$ ， respectively， while the $\mathsf{H R P}@2\mathsf{D}$ MSMOFs biohybrids maintained $91.0\%$ ， $83.4\%$ and $75.3\%$ of its original activity because of the tight confinement.[17] Organic solvent-susceptibility is a main obstacle that limits enzymes in industrial catalysis. As anticipated,2D MSMOFs improve the durability of embedded enzymes against organic solvents including dimethyl sulfoxide (DMsO) and DMF, even though the resistance was limited (Figure 4A). This phenomenon was caused by the fact that organic solvent molecules denature proteins not only by unfolding effect but also by penetrating into the active sites and changing the local environment.[34] Specifically, the catalytic ability of free HRP was almost completely lost after DMF or DMSO treatments, while HRP@2D MSMOFs still well retained its catalytic power (Figure S17 and Table S4).
In order to demonstrate the activity reservation was attributted by the structural stabilization of protein confined in 2D MSMOFs,we designed another experiment wherein the bovine serum albumin (BSA)-scaffolded gold nanocluste [35] was embeded within the 2D MSMOFs (Figure 4B). The as-synthesized BSA-scaffolded gold nanocluste (BSA-AuCNs) possessed a red emission $(\lambda_{\mathrm{em}}\ m a x{=}660$ nm)owing to spatial confinement of free electrons in BSA-directed gold nanoclusters (Figure S18A to S18C). After encapsulated it within 2D MSMOFs, the luminescent property was well maintained becasuce of the mild encapsulation method (Figure S19A-S19D). When exposing BSA-AuCNs to high concentration urea, organic solvent (eg. DMF） and high temperature $(100~^{\circ}\mathsf{C})$ ，respectively, the fluorescence intensity gradually reduced to $62.7\%$ ， $57.9\%$ and $1.02\%$ ， respectively (The pink line in Figure 4C and Figure S20A). These were predictable because protein scaffolds could be unfolded in such conditions and leaded to the aggregation of AuCNs that quench the fluorescence. On the contrary, all of the 2D MsMOFs-encapsulated BSA-AuCNs (denoted as BSA-AuCNs $@$ MSMOFs) maintained more than $90\%$ fluorescence efficiency upon similar treatments (The blue line in Figure 4C and Figure S2oB). Meanwhile, it was also confirmed that the 2D MSMOFs layer itself is structurally stable in urea, DMF and after heating (Figure 4D). In addition, a further ${\sf H}_{2}{\sf O}_{2}$ -induced quenching experiment, where the ${\sf H}_{2}{\sf O}_{2}$ diffused into the interior and quenched AuCNs through oxidation, also confirm the accessibly of the encapsulated BSA-AuCNs within 2D MSMOFs biohybrids (Figure 4E). These results together ascertained that the shielding against unfolding by 2D MsMOFs endowed the hosted protenis with high stability, and simultaneously retained their functionalities.
## Biocatalysis and stimulus-responsive MOFs “cell mimic"
The improved bioactivity as well as durability of biomacromolecule protected by 2D MSMOFs inspired us to explore its practicability in organic-phase biocatalysis. HRP is a peroxidase that enables to catalyze the oxidation of aromatic amine in an environmental friendly route[36,37] The constructed HRP $@20$ MSMOFs biocatalyst displayed an increased catalytic ability for aromatic amine oxidation in DMF, compared with that using HRP $@30$ MOFs (Figure S21A). The absorption maximum of the oxidized aromatic amine appeared ca. $450\mathsf{n m}$ (Figure S22A), which may be ascribed to the formation of the low-polymerized aromatic amine due to the coupling reaction in enzymatic catalysis.[38] In addition, the crystal structure of HRP $@20$ MSMOFs was well maintained after catalysis. (Figure S22B and S22C), and some nanofiber-like aromatic amine polymer was observed under SEM imaging (Figure S22D).
Biocatalytic cascades confined in cellular environment represent a major class of chemical transformations that enables the biological signal transduction and metabolic pathways in an orderly way. Mimicking the cellular biocascades allows the localized and programmed reactions process,which have been employed in novel biomedical applications such as microreactors and biosensors.[39-42] Inspired by this, a glucose-stimulated multi-responsive “cell mimic" (CM)was constructed through co-confinement of the biorecognition unit (GOx was used) and biosignal transmission unit (BTU) within 2D MSMOFs (Figure 5A). Herein, we chose BSA-scaffolded gold nanocluster as the BTU, because gold nanocluster possesses the peroxidase-like activity (Figure S23A) and luminescence property simultaneously (Figure S23B), which may afford the multiple signal response in single“cell mimic". The Uv-vis and fluorescence spectrum test indicated almost $100\%$ BSA-AuCNs and GOx were encapsulated within the 2D MSMOFs hybrid using our strategy (Figure S24), and SEM imaging reveal that the boomerang-like 2D MSMOFs CM was also assembled by spindle-shaped sheets,which was analogous to the spindle-shaped cell such as smooth muscle cells (The inserted SEM image in Figure 5A and Figure S25). When glucose was added into the constructed 2D MSMOFs CM, the biocascade communication was activated. Glucose was firstly recognized by $60\times$ and yielded ${\sf H}_{2}{\sf O}_{2}$ ，and the generated ${\sf H}_{2}{\sf O}_{2}$ acts as a substrate for AuCNs,which can not only catalyse TMB into a blue product (oxTMB） through peroxidase-like property of BSA-AuCNs, but also oxidize AuCNs that leads to fluorescence quenching. As a result, the constructed MSMOFs CM enabled the glucose-responsive dual signal transduction: 1) chrominance “trun-on", and 2) fluorescence “turn-off" (Figure 5A and Figure S26). Interestingly, the visual discrimination of these two signal readouts was complementary, wherein the sensitive region for chrominance “trun-on" was $1.0{-}10.0\ \mathrm{mM}$ glucose while the sensitive region of fluorescence “turn-off" was $0.1{-}1.0~\mathrm{mM}$ glucose (Figure 5B). In addition, good linearities between the signal intensities and the concentrations of glucose were observed (Figure 5C). It indicated that the visual sensing with higher resolution was achieved by using dual responsive MSMOFs CM. To verify the advantages of 2DMSMOFs nanostructure on the biocascade communication mimicking,we also constructed the 3D microporous MOFs CM using the similar strategy (Figure S27). The biocascade communication in 3D microporous MOFs CM, evaluated by the fluorescence responsive rate after activation by glucose, was much slower than that in the 2D MSMOFs CM (Figure S28). Such inhibition on signal response was expectable because the intercommunication for biocascade was suffocated in 3D microporous architecture.
## Conclusion
In conclusion, we impart a biocompatible, peptides-directed strategy that enables to tailor the MOFs-shrouded biohybrids into controllable nanoarchitectures in a simple manner, and also highlight that the importance of the designed MOFs architectures for maintaining the biofunctionality of the obtained nanobiohybrids. The novel 2D MSMOFs biohybrids shows significant enhancement in activity compared with the widely explored 3D microporous MOFs biocomposites， attributing by the shortened diffusion path and enlarged pore channel that facilitates the biotransformation. Meanwhile, the designed 2D MSMOFs coating endows the embedded biomacromolecule as well as its biomineral with augmented biofunctionality, and allows to perform cellular-mimicking activities in uninhabitable conditions. Our findings herein afford a new insight to construct the robust functional MOFs biosystem with excellent bioactivity as well as durability,which may advance the artificial cells construction and accelerate the cell-free biotransformation in sophisticated applications.
